      "math_academy_id": "q-1262",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "For the sets $Z=\\{-1,0,1\\}$ and $Y=Z\\times Z,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nI. $(-1,0,1)\\in Y$\n\nII. $(-1,1)\\in Y$\n\nIII. $(0,0)\\in Y$",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $Z\\times Z$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $Z$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Z.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${Z}^{2}=Z\\times Z$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14123139/assets/6cb962e74701db361807c237a521f13a1c753e4acc6d68a1cfb1694bdfbd45bc.png)\n\nHence, the set $Y=Z\\times Z$ is given by\n\n$$\nY={(-1,-1),(-1,0),(-1,1),(0,-1),(0,0),(0,1),(1,-1),(1,0),(1,1)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
